{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1299908-tow-vs-shaped-projection","id":1299908,"title":"Tow vs Shaped Projection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-26T05:08:23-07:00","id":1299908,"title":"Tow vs Shaped Projection","content":"Does the Tow power really limit you to only increasing your size parameter by a maximum of 1? So if you have Telekinesis 3 you can only spend extra successes to get yourself up to size 2? Shaped Projection can go all the way to size 3 with extra successes. It's worded funny. It says &quot;every 2 successes allow,&quot; but then says &quot;by a maximum of.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I was thinking of an Aesculapian emergency responder who has Psychokinesis and it seems like Perikinesis 3/Telekinesis 1 is the way to go for that character)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T05:17:16-07:00","id":1300236,"title":"","content":"The way it is written is a little weird... but I would say to can increase by +1 for 2 successes and that\u2019s all.<br /> Shaped Projection can go up to 3, even proxies can\u2019t go further than this, while tow can go up to standard size +1, that\u2019s 4 to 5 dots and 5 to 7 dots... if you have 3 dots on one of them Tow would move up to size 3, the same as Shaped Projection, ignoring all the other advantages of 3 dots in each of them, the results are the same...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T01:49:42-07:00","id":1300496,"title":"","content":"Tow is meant to be slow but strong. You can spend the 2 successes to increase your Size parameter by +1. That might not seem like much when you\u2019re a low Psi character, but it\u2019s more than you could otherwise lift. Even beginner PKs can lift a motorcycle with it, most can pick up a city bus (or a jet fighter), whereas non-proxies can pick up a submarine! Proxies themselves can pick up a naval destroyer, or if they apply Kinetic Mastery to it can pick up an aircraft carrier.<br /> <br /> Shaped projection is cool as well but caps out at Size 3 (except with Kinetic Mastery) and costs Psi points. You can use Tow even in after a drawn out fight where you\u2019ve used up all your psionic reserves but still need to hold up that shattered wall long enough for the civilians to escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}